sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch04-24> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch04-24--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch04-24--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch04-24: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.61" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.615"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.66"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Morphospace position between living groups is a concrete variable, and many published matrices already combine fossil and living taxa. Those matrices cover vertebrates and shelly invertebrates far better than the full tree of life, so the scope is partial. The analysis is standard but slow to harmonize, and character choice can nudge fossils toward intermediate scores." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Place fossil species in morphospace and on trees with living members of the same groups, and ask whether fossils occupy positions between living subgroups more often than a random-extinction null. An excess of intermediate placements would confirm the claim; fossils nested inside living subgroups as often as that null would refute a general intermediate-stem pattern." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Character matrices are clade-specific and unevenly published.", "Stem-group fossils are expected to look intermediate under the hypothesis being tested, which can shade into circular coding.", "Soft-bodied and poorly fossilized groups are almost absent." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch04-24--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch04-24--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch04-24--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch04-24--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch04-24 by Grok 4.7: 0.72" ;
